Context: T016 formal model of authorization, pairing, and revocation (authorization rules in ARCHITECTURE.md). Design choices recorded in tla/README.md and NOTES.md: monotone history variables (srcEverOwned, revokedEver, annRowSes) make immovability checkable as cardinality bounds, because a move overwrites its own trace; invitation expiry is a nondeterministic action, not a clock (consumption must race expiry; TTL length is configuration); revocation is final per device identity because a revoked identity consuming a fresh invitation would falsify the stated safety property; orphaned sources stay locked. The per-request registry check stays in Authorized although redundant in-model: real connection teardown is not atomic with in-flight requests; the single hub writer serializes both. Six one-line mutations verified non-vacuousness; one survived by design (an active device consuming a second invitation breaks no stated property; the absent guard blocks it anyway). Safety-only model: pairing liveness is device reconnection, owned by Sync.tla's eventual-reconnection assumption. T018 must implement this state machine; revisit the spec with any rule change. Logs in $LOOPER_ARTIFACT_DIR/t016-tla/.
